[
  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Practice and the Dojo. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 10: Gary Bernhardt from SCNA 2012 / RailsConf (2012).",
  "Gary's legendary SCNA and RailsConf lightning talks and screencasts set the gold standard for terminal fluency and testing velocity in the Chicago developer community.",
  "What inspired Gary Bernhardt's obsession with sub-second feedback loops and terminal minimalism? How did 'WAT' and 'Destroy All Software' reshape an entire generation of developers? What principles guided Gary Bernhardt when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: g6gFCr5isGg). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "Fast feedback loops remain the ultimate competitive advantage. If your test suite takes 10 minutes to run, multi-agent iteration loops grind to a halt. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "Thank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 11. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]